      "writtenOn": "2022-03-28T16:30:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes - the key is still the typeface ID, and there is only one cache entry per typeface.\n\nThe hb_font in the cache represents the parts of an hb_font that are based only on attributes of the SkTypeface (the hb_face, plus the variation design position).  You still need to call hb_font_create_sub_font for the attributes that are in the SkFont.\n\nThe goal is to avoid constructing the parent hb_font and calling getVariationDesignPosition/hb_font_set_variations on every call to ShaperHarfBuzz::shape.\n\nImplementations like SkTypeface_Mac::onGetVariationDesignPosition may still be doing nontrivial work even with https://skia.googlesource.com/skia.git/+show/e85afc2b18212360b9be8e6ca8c786b4ec6348b5.  And AFAICT that work will yield the same results on every call for a given typeface and does not need to be repeated for each shaping.",
      "parentUuid": "0a3090ed_875e52bb",
      "revId": "8f0e4339386fe9722d7b268a282b1ff6da120a8a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25a07c6f_f6eb19fd",
        "filename": "modules/skshaper/src/SkShaper_harfbuzz.cpp",
